  "aiSummary": "This bill allows Madison County's Sheriff's Office to enter into agreements with three neighboring Tennessee counties (Unicoi, Greene, and Cocke) to conduct joint law enforcement operations across state lines. The agreements must specify how liability for damages will be handled and must be reported annually to the North Carolina Department of Justice.",
  "aiProArguments": "Supporters argue this bill improves public safety by enabling regional law enforcement cooperation in a border area where criminals and emergencies don't respect state lines. Cross-border coordination can make operations more efficient and effective, and the liability-sharing requirements protect both states and counties while allowing officers to work together on specialized missions.",
  "aiConArguments": "Opponents may be concerned about potential liability exposure for North Carolina and Madison County despite the bill's protections, or worry that agreements with other states could complicate oversight and accountability. Some might question whether the broad language around \"special operations missions\" and \"cooperative law enforcement actions\" provides sufficient clarity about what activities are permitted.",
